      "type": "text",
      "text": "Both evals pass. The work is in two commits on `reqforge/TASK-0044` and is ready for review.\n\n**What changed**\n- **AC1, the field:** tasks now have `next_action` (at most 280 characters, and it must name a file path, a command or a record id) and `next_action_set` (a `YYYY-MM-DD` date). When `next_action` changes, the date is set to today unless the same write changes the date itself. This applies to direct edits and to changesets.\n- **AC2, `NEXT:` capture:** when an agent run ends, the last `NEXT:` line in its final message is saved on the task as a pending proposal, along with the run id. It goes into the same commit as the run log and appears in the run's result. Accept, edit or reject it with the new `POST /api/tasks/{id}/next-action` route. Accept and edit set the date to today; reject leaves the current next action alone. The agent prompt now tells the agent to end with a `NEXT:` line.\n- **AC3, shown first:** the brief already put the next action first. The task drawer now opens with a Next action panel showing the text and \"set YYYY-MM-DD\", with the pending proposal and Accept / Edit / Reject under it.\n- **AC4, chat wrap-up:** after a changeset has been applied in a chat session, closing the panel or clicking New asks the chat agent once for updated next actions and a new Next item for the project snapshot. New shows \"Wrapping up…\" and starts the fresh session when that reply finishes. The answer is an ordinary changeset that the user applies or rejects.\n\n**Evals and tests run**\n- **E1:** `cargo test --manifest-path server/Cargo.toml --test context -- next_action` passes. That is 8 new `next_action_*` tests; all 17 tests in the file pass, and the full server test suite and clippy are clean.\n- **E2:** `node web/e2e/run.mjs --junit web/e2e/results/junit-next-action.xml --suite next-action` passes 42/42, on two separate runs.\n- The neighbouring e2e suites (core, agent-start, task-start, task-complete) still pass: 145/145 checks.\n- The web UI type-checks, builds and lints clean.\n\n**Things to look at in review**\n- **Validation rule:** \"names a file path, command or record id\" is a pattern match. It looks for an id like `TASK-0001`, a path with a slash or a known file extension, or a backtick-quoted or common command.\n- **Bad `NEXT:` lines:** a `NEXT:` line is stored as a proposal even if it breaks the rules; it is only checked when the user accepts or edits it.\n- **`web/dist`:** I rebuilt and committed it, as earlier UI tasks did. Building it meant running `npm ci` inside `web/` in this worktree.\n- **Fake agents:** the e2e fake agent now handles `PROPOSE-NEXT`, `NEXT-DEMO` and the wrap-up message. The fake Claude in `server/tests/context.rs` can also act as a coding agent.\n- **Existing race:** a changeset card's \"I applied…\" follow-up can land in the next session if New is clicked before it is sent. That predates this task and I left it alone; the e2e suite waits for the follow-up.\n- **Snapshot banner:** the missing-snapshot banner described in the design doc is still not in the chat panel, and I didn't add it because it's outside this task.\n\nThe `reqforge` MCP server failed to start, so I read the requirements from the brief and the design docs in `requirements/design/` instead. The claude.ai Google Calendar connector needs to be authorized in your claude.ai connector settings, but this task didn't use it."
